$f'(x) = 2x(x - 6)^{2} + 2x^{2}(x - 6)$
$= 2x(x - 6)(x - 6 + x)$
$= 4x(x - 6)(x - 3)$
$x = 0$, $x = 6$ or $x = 3$
$f(0) = 0$, $f(6) = 0$, $f(3) = 9 \times 9 = 81$
Expanding, $f'(x) = 4x^{3} - 36x^{2} + 72x$, so $f''(x) = 12x^{2} - 72x + 72$.
$f''(0) = 72 > 0$, so $(0, 0)$ is a local minimum.
$f''(6) = 432 - 432 + 72 = 72 > 0$, so $(6, 0)$ is a local minimum.
$f''(3) = 108 - 216 + 72 = -36 < 0$, so $(3, 81)$ is a local maximum.
